      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.11.0_FA.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.11.0 \u2014 \u06cc\u0627\u062f\u062f\u0627\u0634\u062a \u0646\u0633\u062e\u0647",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.11.0_FA.md",
      "line": 8,
      "text": "- \u067e\u0633 \u0627\u0632 \u067e\u0627\u06cc\u0627\u0646\u060c \u0647\u0634\u062f\u0627\u0631\u0647\u0627\u06cc ZAP \u0628\u0647\u200c\u06cc\u0627\u0641\u062a\u0647\u200c\u0647\u0627\u06cc Sentinel \u062a\u0628\u062f\u06cc\u0644 \u0645\u06cc\u200c\u0634\u0648\u0646\u062f \u0648 context \u0645\u0648\u0642\u062a \u062d\u0630\u0641 \u0645\u06cc\u200c\u0634\u0648\u062f.",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.11.1_FA.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.11.1",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.14.0.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.14.0",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.14.1.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.14.1",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.0.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.15.0",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.0.md",
      "line": 7,
      "text": "Explicit failed matcher records and error events never become vulnerabilities. Their count is recorded and the import is marked PARTIAL. Other imported matches remain SCANNER_REPORTED and require independent validation. An absent matcher-status field is accepted for older exports; this does not establish validation. The export schema supplies no scanner version, so Sentinel does not invent one.",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.1.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.15.1",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.2.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.15.2",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.2.md",
      "line": 9,
      "text": "The existing background import transaction saves no assessment when validation fails. Error messages explain the unsupported structure. This is validation of Sentinel's supported import subset, not a complete SARIF conformance checker.",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.2.md",
      "line": 13,
      "text": "Imported numeric security severity contributes to the mapped severity only when it is finite and within 0 through 10. Infinity, NaN, oversized integers, booleans and values outside that range are ignored; the source text severity then applies. An explicit zero score maps to informational, including a SARIF result whose level is error. Positive scores below 4 map to LOW, including 0.1 and 0.9 that ",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.3.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.15.3",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.4.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.15.4",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.5.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.15.5",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.15.5.md",
      "line": 9,
      "text": "Only the initial response has this additional status policy. Missing sensitive-file probes commonly return non-success responses; those alone do not imply a failed assessment. Redirects remain disabled, and Sentinel does not store or contact a redirect destination from the Location header.",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.16.0.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.16.0",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.17.0.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.17.0",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.17.0.md",
      "line": 23,
      "text": "Primary design references: [OWASP authorization testing](https://owasp.github.io/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/stable/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/05-Authorization_Testing/02-Testing_for_Bypassing_Authorization_Schema), [OWASP business logic testing](https://wstg.owasp.org/stable/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/10-Business_Logic_Testing/), and [Invicti's explanation of XSS valida",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.18.0.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.18.0",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.18.0.md",
      "line": 11,
      "text": "The new application icon is an original code-drawn obsidian shield with a luminous infinity mark. OPEN SENTINEL.exe in the project root launches this version's portable EXE without a command window. Its C# source is included. Keep the full portable folder and its _internal directory together. Browser shutdown is bounded using only the disposable browser process verified as a child of the scanner; ",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.19.0.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam Sentinel 0.19.0",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.19.0.md",
      "line": 15,
      "text": "Primary references: https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.4.html and https://www.zaproxy.org/docs/desktop/addons/openapi-support/ . Sentinel implements the explicitly documented subset, not all capabilities of those projects.",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.19.1.md",
      "line": 1,
      "text": "# Qolam_Hacker 0.19.1 \u2014 evidence and coverage upgrade",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/RELEASE_NOTES_0.20.0.md",
      "line": 5,
      "text": "- New frozen installations use `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\III85III\\OBSIDIAN`. Existing portable or per-user `Qolam Sentinel` databases are used in place. No history, settings or credentials are copied, reset or renamed.",
      "category": "historical_record"
    },
    {
